      "type": "text",
      "text": ">2 mo w toxicity · dehydration or ⍉PO intake: parenteral third-gen cephalosporin (ex ceftriaxone) - cefazolin if local pathogens sensitive - aminoglycosides (ex gentamicin, potentially nephrotoxic) for complex UTIs. Blood cx neg & good response: PO step-down (ex cefixime · cephalexin · TMP-SMX · amoxicillin/clavulanate) to complete 7- to 10-day course - FQ only for selected children (ex >1 y w complicated MDR gram-negative UTI)"
     }
